## Custom

Pick **Custom** and set the colours under **Colours for the custom theme**:
the panels, the writing, the accent (the selected thing, the main button,
prices) and the four meaning colours. Keep the writing clearly lighter or
darker than the panels. **Panel solidity** at 1 hides the world behind a
panel; **Lettering** chooses between the old-style titles, a book serif, or
plain letters; **Corner rounding** at 0 keeps the square Poggy corners.

## A script that should keep its own colours

Add its product id to **Scripts that keep their own colours**, for example
`poggy_supplydrops`. Its screens go back to how they looked before.

## When it changes

poggy_core's own menus and /poggy change at once. A script's screens take the
new look the next time they open.

Screens drawn with pictures keep their art. The fishing HUD (brass) and the
market (leather) ship with a picture skin: set that script's own skin setting
to `default` to give it the theme instead.

## Each player's own screens: /poggyui

Every player can type **/poggyui** to set, for their own screen only:

- **Size**: every Poggy screen from 50% to 200%. **Fit my screen** picks the
  size that suits their resolution (useful on 1440p and 4K monitors, where
  screens made for 1080p look small); **Reset to 100%** goes back.
- **Look**: the server's theme, or **Light**, a light parchment theme that is
  easier to read for some players.
- **Less motion**: no sliding, fading or spinning on any Poggy screen.

A sample screen shows each change as it is made. Their choice is kept on their
own PC for this server, and every Poggy screen takes it the next time it opens.
A size never makes a screen's area smaller than 1280x720, so a 1080p screen
goes up to 150%.

**Players may pick a theme** (under Theme, off unless you turn it on) also
lists the ready-made themes in /poggyui, so a player can wear one for
themselves. Custom is never offered, and scripts on **Scripts that keep their
own colours** keep them for everyone.
